        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the majority of points (at least 53 out of 104 available).',
          gameplay: "Dealer deals all 16 cards one at a time (4 each). Player to dealer's left leads. Must follow suit; all trumps count as one suit. Must beat the highest card in the trick if possible. Winner of each trick leads to the next. Four tricks; team with at least 53 of 104 points wins. Tie 52-52: side that announced last double loses, or if no double the old team or lone player loses.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit; all trumps count as one suit.',
            'Must beat the highest card in the trick if possible.',
            'Winner of each trick leads to the next.',
            'Objective: take at least 53 of 104 card points (A=11, 10=10, Q=3, J=2).',
            'Partnerships: holders of the two black Queens are partners, or declarer plays alone (Wesele, Zolo, Zolo Du).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Identify your partner! In a Normal Game, watch who plays the black Queens. If you don't have one, your partner is the other person who doesn't play one.",
          intermediate: "The 'Ten' Flush: Since Tens are worth 10 points and are high trumps, use your top three trumps (â™¥A, â™£10, â™ 10) to 'flush' the remaining Tens out of the opponents' hands as early as possible.",
          advanced: 'Zolo Du (Solo Tout) Detection: If you see someone bid Solo Tout, they almost certainly hold the top three trumps. Your only hope is to hold the 4th top trump (â™¥10) and wait to trap their lead.',
          tips: [
            'Card points in the entire game total exactly 104. Knowing you have 52 points means you only need 1 more to avoid a tie.',
            'A tie (52-52) in some variants means the defenders win; check house rules.',
          ],
